turnip: darwin backend failures reach stderr in a release build (piano natively, tooling/metal)

- A release build's vk_log is silent (no debug messenger, MESA_VK_LOG 0, !MESA_DEBUG): a lost device said nothing, so a native Metal
  client's loss had no reason anywhere. _vk_device_set_lost and _vk_queue_set_lost now also write the reason (with the kernel call
  and its IOReturn the backend puts in it) once per device / queue with mesa_loge, on stderr: with the kernel's stderr-log=1 it is a
  console line "fd2: pid N <process>: MESA: error: device lost (<file>:<line>): <reason>". Apple builds only.
- Every kernel method that fails is named on stderr, the first time per method and status in the process and then at the 10th,
  100th, ... failure ("NativeAdreno: kernel BoAlloc failed: 0xe00002bd (1 time)"); the answers the backend expects are left out
  (a WaitFence slice's kIOReturnTimeout, Submit/BoFree kIOReturnBusy, GetStatus kIOReturnUnsupported). The virtio-gpu path is
  untouched.
- "darwin: no GPU address range" (a full client window) is written the first time and then every 10th, 100th, ... time.
Against the tree after 0001 and 0002. MIT, as the files.

